invariant: INV-11
file: handshake_flight.c
catches: webpki_session_aes
reason: the client writes the HelloRetryRequest's synthetic message at
  SHA-256 whatever suite the retry names, so after a retry that selects
  TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 its transcript holds a 32-byte message_hash
  where RFC 9846 §4.4.1 puts Hash.length bytes, and every secret after
  it differs from the server's. The session test's AES-256 retry row
  reaches the certificate only when both ends agree.

--- old
        hsr_restart_transcript(h, hsr_suite_hash_len(h), raw, raw_len);
--- new
        hsr_restart_transcript(h, SHA256_LEN, raw, raw_len);
